      "text": "To determine how many integers Josef could pick such that Timothy's quotient is an integer, we need to find the divisors of 1000. The steps are as follows:\n\n1. Identify the number whose divisor is calculated as an integer.\n2. List out all divisors of 1000.\n3. Count those divisors.\n4. Print the count of divisors.\n\nLet's start by finding the divisors of 1000 using Python code.\n```python\ndef number_of_divisors(n):\r\n    divisors = []\r\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\r\n        if n % i == 0:\r\n            divisors.append(i)\r\n    return divisors\r\n\r\n# Calculate the number of divisors of 1000\r\nresult = number_of_divisors(1000)\r\nprint((result, len(result)))\n```\n```output\n([1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 20, 25, 40, 50, 100, 125, 200, 250, 500, 1000], 16)\n```\nThe divisors of 1000 are \\(1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 10, 20, 25, 40, 50, 100, 125, 200, 250, 500,\\) and \\(1000\\). \n\nThe number of such divisors is \\(16\\). \n\nThus, the number of integers Josef could pick such that Timothy's quotient is an integer is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
